                {
                    Name = "Stellenbosh University",
                    PartnerShortDescription = "SU",
                    PartnerLongDescription = "Stellenbosch University (SU) is a prestigious academic institution established\r\nin 1918, located in South Africa. It operates across multiple campuses,\r\nincluding Stellenbosch and Tygerberg, offering a wide range of\r\nundergraduate and postgraduate programs. The University has three core\r\nprocesses: research, teaching, and community service. Stellenbosch\r\nUniversity consists of 139 departments across 10 faculties: Agri Sciences, Arts\r\nand Social Sciences, Economic and Management Sciences, Education,\r\nEngineering, Law, Medicine & Health Sciences, Military Science, Science, and\r\nTheology. It also includes specialized schools, including the Stellenbosch\r\nBusiness School and School for Data Science & Computational Thinking.\r\nSU is known for its strong research focus, particularly in medical sciences,\r\nand collaborates with entities like the National Health Laboratory Service\r\n(NHLS) on projects such as RR-TB testing. The university's funding primarily\r\ncomes from student fees, government subsidies, and research grants. SU\r\nfaces challenges related to institutional transformation and financial\r\nsustainability, with a growing reliance on student fees. Despite these\r\nchallenges, SU remains a leading institution in South Africa, committed to\r\nacademic excellence and global engagement through programs like the\r\nGlobal Education Programme. The university's financial health is closely tied\r\nto its ability to manage these funding streams effectively while navigating\r\nbroader economic and social challenges in South Africa.",
